# stage 2: $0060-$015F, decrypted by boot0 from $0850-$094F (EOR $A5). A chain of RTSes through the
# stack page. Only $0060-$010F is here: $0110-$015F comes from $0900-$094F, which the PROM didn't load.
source ../mem/stage2.bin
include apple2.sym
$0000 org $0000
$0000 skip $60
$0060 code
$0060 label READ_STAGE3
$0060 comment in: A = X = 4 (from SET_PROLOGUE). Reads 4 sectors with the PROM's ReadSector
$0060 note $3E = 4 (left in A2L)
$0062 note $3A = 4
$0064 note sector count
$0068 note BOOT_PAGE: $0400
$006A comment $0801 = RTS: the PROM's ReadSector ends with JMP $0801, so it now returns here
$006F comment $7C = $Cn: the JSR below becomes JSR $Cn5C (ReadSector)
$007A label NEXT_SECTOR
$007B operand $005C
$007D note always: ReadSector's CMP $0800 (1 sector) leaves C = 1. What follows is a decoy
$007F db $2A
$007F note never run: a 4-and-4 data reader, to mislead
$00A9 label SECTOR_DONE
$00AD comment RTS -> next return address in the chain
$00AE db 6
$00AE note never run
$00B4 code
$00B4 label SET_PROLOGUE
$00B4 comment $00-$03 = D4 D5 D6 D7 (read by nothing we know of), A = X = 4
$00C5 db $3B
$00C5 note junk (the decrypted rest of boot0's sector)
$0100 comment the chain: each word + 1 is where the next RTS goes
$0100 rts 4
$0104 note the loader: $0400 is an RTS, $0401 a JMP $0406
$0108 dw 4
$0108 note junk, never popped
